> I used rawrite under win98/dos to make these disks.
> After hooking up my alpha, inserting the milo disk.. following the steps
in
> the
> alpha addendum supplied by RH i get my milo disk to boot.. and after what
> looks like a lil reboot i see my milo prompt.
> This is where i get stuck.
> I remove the milo disk, insert the kernel disk and type: boot floppy

Aha, here you go wrong. There is no such thing as "floppy", so MILO
simply does not know what you want.

> The only thing milo tells me when i do that is:
> MILO: unknown filesystem on device void
> MILO: Failed to load the kernel

That's because MILO doesn't know what you're talking about :-)

> Can anyone tell me what i'm doing wrong? Did i make the wrong disks, am i
> using
> the wrong command here??

You use the correct disks. The MILO command is wrong. The correct
syntax is (with the bootdisk in the drive):

MILO> boot fd:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

Then insert the root floppy when asked for.

Martin Sinot
