> but is this a good idea? Anyone tried it? What is sound quality coming out of
> these little things?

The Multia is fast enough to decode MP3 files, but the internal sound
card has poor quality (at least compared to my Turtle Beach Tropez
in my PC, both directly connected to the HiFi amplifier). 
You should consider adding a better PCI sound card, but probably
you need the space for a second hard disk.  
Another aspect is that the Multia needs the CPU cooler, which 
means a considerable background noise.
But the Multia is probably the cheapest way to build a dedicated
MP3 player.

