The Alpha systems are top of the line with SpecFP95 you can see the
benchmarks on www.comaq.com
There is however 1 small problem in your case when you choose to run Linux
you alse have the Linux math libs these aren't really code the wat that you
get 100% of the Alpha's abilities. There are however smarter libs to use the
FP instruction set better. The best solution would be to buy the Fortran or
C compilers from Compaq these are currently in beta fase on Linux. Or you
could buy the 99$ non-commercial release of True64.

Fortran is available in the Linux distro's for Alpha also, but with less FP
power due to the lack of good math libs. You can fix this by buying or
compiling your code on a Fortran compiler from DEC/Compaq.

Raymond


