Bal Soora <bssoora@mmm.com> wrote:
: I am considering using a Multia as a dedicated MP3 player. It has a sound card
: but is this a good idea? Anyone tried it? What is sound quality coming out of
: these little things?
The UDB/Noname/Multia as at least fast enough for MP3 decoding at 44.1kHz
stereo 16 bit. The quality of the builtin soundcard is OK; not the best but
OK. If you use a decent hifi amplifier this should be OK.
But you should remember that the UDBs have a little heat problem and having
it running long time could cause premature death. I know of two UDBs that
died that way :(
So watch out for good cooling with enough airflow.

: Bal.
