Michael DuFresne (xdufresn@raytheon.com) wrote:
: I am hoping to play with the software RAID features of AdvFS.

You are thinking about LSM (Logical Storage Manager), not about AdvFS. AdvFS
on its own can have file systems spanning several disks, but not real RAID.
Unless CPQ changed the licensing terms recently, most of RAID capabilities
of LSM are extra-cost. I think you can have disk catenation without the 
licences, but mirroring, striping, and graphical interface all require the
licence. (Won't be the first time I am wrong, though - CPQ seems to inherited
the Digital's trait of not knowing that they are going to do next month).

In any case, the RAID functionality of the Linux md devices appears to be
on par with the DU LSM software RAID, at least from the md manual pages.

