> I've a problem??
> I've installed linux debian potato on my alpha pc but.
> 
> When i rebooted i got (and still get) the following error messages (it
> nearly gets there...):
> 
> INIT: id "3" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> INIT: id "2" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> INIT: id "6" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> INIT: id "1" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> INIT: id "4" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> INIT: id "3" respawning too fast: disabled for five minutes
> 
> ...etc            (this is the real problem)
> 
> It just keeps scrolling on with these 'INIT' messages every 4-10 seconds.

It's not dangerous ;-)

The processes listed in /etc/inittab on the lines beginning with 1: till
6: 
terminate immediately after init, the mother of all processes, spawns
them.
Usually this is /sbin/getty, the program that initializes the console
and lets
you login.  You can run getty by hand to find out what the problem is.

do 
/sbin/getty 38400 tty10 
or so, and watch what happens.

Apparently you do have access to your system, presumably not on the
console then.  Maybe you
don't have a console (no keyboard, no vga card?)

In that case: comment out the lines from /etc/inittab that start getty,
and you'll be fine.

Hope that helps
-- 
Luuk  van  Dijk



