I just answered a similar question in this newsgroup: Respawning Error
what to do.

init, the mother of all processes can't start /sbin/getty.  I have no
idea why,
but if you can access the system over the network you could find out by
running it by hand.
But then again: if this is your first boot after installing you probably
can't....hmmm

You could try to boot from the debian rescue floppy, mount your root and
try to run /sbin/getty by
hand to find out what goes wrong. 

to boot the rescue image type 'rescue' at the boot prompt (the first one
you get)
then

	mount -r /dev/<your root device> /mnt
	cd /mnt/sbin
	./getty 38400 tty7

if that works, switch to console 7 (alt-f7) and look for a login prompt

Post your findings and we may find some more clues.

Hope this helps
