Hi,
I have the suspicion that there is a (well hidden) bug somewhere in the Linux
network code causing hangs on the Alpha (not on x86...). I can't prove it (not 
yet), but I have some strong hints:

An Alpha (EB164, 500Mhz), formerly running flawlessly in a small private network,
mysteriously hangs after connected to our university's network. We've changed the
mainboard, RAM modules, the power supply, disks, VGA card, network cards and of 
course kernel versions (2.2.3 to 2.2.13). No success, still hangs, the box 
wasn't up for more than hour at best. So we switched off and threw the box in a 
corner...

Then, after some time, we tried again, but now (accidently) behind a firewall. 
No problems, the system was running very stable. Re-connection to the 'big'
network, and it crashed within minutes.

Has anybody seen a similar behavior or are there some suggestions what the cause 
can be?

We plan to investigate into this deeper next week, maybe we can isolate the bug. 
A switch doesn't help, the broadcast traffic (IP, ICMP, IPX, Netware, 
Appletalk etc) seems to be the problem :-( 

