I bought an AXPpci33 21066 Alpha two days ago and installed Red Hat on it.

It has indeed even more bugs and misconfigurations than Red Hat for Intel.

There's no control whatsoever to choose specific packages in the setup
program,
only which categories (C development libraries etc.). When the install
completes,
only less important stuff like Gnome are installed. Important things like
mtools, bzip2
and a lot of other crucial admin programs aren't installed.

Since my RAM didn't have parity, I had to buy 16 MB parity SIMMs, but the
system
is super slow. I know it's a board+CPU from 1994, but a 166 Mhz Alpha
should really
be faster than a Pentium 75 that I now have, right?

I hope Slackware will sooner or later come out for Alpha.

Greetz,

      Raydar.

