I have the same board, get more RAM!!! No Alpha is of much use/fun when
it has < 64MB RAM. You should shoot for something over 64MB. A lot of
people run 90MB and think it's fine. With Alphas, the more RAM you add
the faster it goes! After 90MB, depending on what you will be
doing/running, the next noticeable performance increase will probably be
at the 128MB mark. Depending on what you are doing, if you can afford it
try and get 128MB in 4 x 32MB and fill all the banks. I believe this
will give you more memory bandwidth.

As for the cache, you should be able to get it from dead 486's.


