Generally, if a Digital UNIX X server understands the graphics
board at all, it "just works"; it dynamically loads the
right DDX code to handle it when it recognizes the display type.
There are some exceptions for certain 3D cards, where you have
to have installed the right bits on top of the base system to
add support (the shared libraies) for that particular board.

Similar capabilities will appear on XFree86 4.0 at long last, due out
in a few months...
