[more of those]

it seems that your /etc/X11/XF86Config doesn't contain a proper
section for your monitor. Just load that file into your favourite
editor and change that section to something like

Section "Monitor"
   Identifier      "My Monitor"
   VendorName      "Unknown"
   ModelName       "Unknown"
   HorizSync       31.5-82
   VertRefresh     40-100

   Modeline "1280x1024"   115.00   1280 1370 1521 1640   1024 1027 1037 1047
   Modeline  "640x480"    45.80 640 672 768 864 480 488 494 530 
EndSection

make sure the Numbers in HorizSync and VertRefresh lines match the
specs of your monitor. The above are from my config file and match my
el-cheapo 17" monitor. Do not just copy this, you might burn your
monitor. HorizSync rates are in kHz while VertRefresh is in 1/second.
Make sure to pick the numbers from your monitor's manual and leave the 
Modelines alone for the beginning.

kind Regards,
