Wim <wim@wanadoo.nl> wrote in message news:80bet5$att$1@news1.xs4all.nl...
> Please help
>
> I have a floppy with linload milo and vmlinux.gz on it.
> How can I boot from this floppydisk?
> I have never installed Linux before on an AXP,  I have a scci cdrom drive
> and a hard drive.
> When I boot from the floppy I get this on my screen
>
>
> VFS Mounted root ( iso9660 filesystem) readonly
> Freeing unused kernel memory 136 k freed
> Warning: unable to open an initial console.
> Kernel panic: No init found. Try passing init= option to kernel.
>
> What should I do to fix this error.
>
> many thanks in advance
>
> Wim

You must have a boot and root floppy ready. Insert the boot
floppy first and boot the kernel with the following command:

MILO> boot fd:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1

Next, insert the root floppy when asked for.

Alternatively, you can boot from CDROM if you have a root filesystem
on CD (I didn't, so I had to use the above command). Type:

MILO> boot fd:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sdX

(where X represents the SCSI device number for your CDROM drive as a
letter, e.g. if the CDROM is on SCSI ID 0, you would type /dev/sda.

And welcome to the Alpha Linux community :-)

Martin Sinot
martin@spase.nl





