> dump -0u -f /dev/st0 -b 64 /homefs
[...]
> The size of homefs is small  and It doesn't need one more volume.
>Is there any problem in my command or any other .....?
>Do you have any idea and any suggestion?

Dump has very old tapes in mind... you can use the s option to
tell dump the size of your tape
ex:
dump -0u -f /dev/st0 -b 64 -s 50000000 /homefs 

By default dump uses 2300 which is on the short side. If you know the dump
will fit on one tape you can use a very large value (as in the example),
otherwise you have to calculate the correct size. 

Jaap



