On Mon, 15 Nov 1999 21:21:13 -0000, Bobby Duvall <jonbob45@hotmail.com> wrote:
>Do you need a special power supply to use a PC164 Alpha motherboard or does
>it just need a standard ATX case?

You need either a power supply that can be switched on without the signal
from the motherboard, or else you need a simple modification to your PC164:
to get mine to work with a standard ATX power supply, I tacked a jumper
across pins 13 and 14 of the power connector. If you hold the motherboard
with the component side facing you and the power connector at the top, those
are the third and fourth pins from the left on the top of the power
connector. When the power cable is plugged in, pin 13 has a black wire, and
pin 14 has a green wire.

*BE CAREFUL!* If you mess this up, you'll likely destroy your power supply,
and maybe your motherboard too.

This modification tells the power supply to be on all the time; most ATX
supplies have a real switch on the back, which can be used to turn the
machine on and off.



