John (plastic@no_spam.oh.verio.com) wrote:

> doing a 'chat -v' gives me nothing. nada.

You should get messages in one of the /var/log files.  If not then
edit /etc/syslog.conf and add

daemon.*                                       /var/log/ppp-log

and then do "touch /var/log/ppp-log", and finally "kill -HUP `pidof
syslogd` to make syslogd reread syslog.conf .  All the messages you
need should appear in /var/log/ppp-log after that.

> --[ chat-ppp0 ]--

> 'ABORT' 'BUSY'
> 'ABORT' 'ERROR'
> 'ABORT' 'NO CARRIER'
> 'ABORT' 'NO DIALTONE'
> 'ABORT' 'Invalid Login'
> 'ABORT' 'Login incorrect'
> 'OK' 'ATZ'
> 'OK' 'ATDT12163770104'
> 'CONNECT' ''

The 'OK' 'ATZ' is wrong.  Change it to  '' ATZ  .  Also change the
'CONNECT' ''  to  CONNECT '\d\c'  to prevent a carriage return that is
otherwise sent and can confuse an ISP.

