Hi,
  I don't think there is a pci version of the permedia 3, just agp.  I
don't know of any alphas that have an agp port.

  In my experience the permedia 2 and permedia 3 have radically
different underlying hardware.  Thus I'd expect its chances of working
to be about the same as any other untested card - not too likely.  (and
that assumes I'm wrong about the agp/pci thing).

  The permedia 2 is a good card, plenty fast enough for any 2d
application, and dirt cheap.  Since there is no serious 3d hardware
accelleration for linux alpha, putting a $200 card like the permedia3 in
an alpha is a waste of money,imo.


