A .bz2 file is a file compressed using the bzip2 compression program. If your
system supports this type of file you can use: bunzip2 file.bz2 or: bzip2 -d
file.bz2

Take a look at: man bzip2 if you need any more info. Bzip2 generally
compresses a bit better than gzip, but with the disadvantage of needing more
RAM and CPU time, and being less supported in general. If you need top rate
compression, though, this is the one you want.

