I think you will save a lot of time if you have the CD.  I tried
installing RH 6.0 without a CD on a PW 600au.  I couldn't get it to
work. It wasn't until after I had installed from a CD that I figured
out that the Tulip driver just doesn't work with my hardware.
[The DE4x5 driver worked OK.]

I found enough documentation on the web to do the job.  Expect
to reread it several times.  RedHat has an extra section for Alphas.
The paper copy you get with the RH package may be a lot more convenient.

I haven't found a really simple way to switch between Linux and Tru64.
Linux needs some boot flags.  I put them in the SRM's boot_osflags
variable.  To boot Tru64 you have to set them back to empty or add
a -flags "" to your boot command (as well as specifying the other disk).

There is more info at:

  http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/srm.html
