X-Deja-AN: 543474322
Organization: My Desk
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


I think I have the problem fixed now.

Originally when I was investigating this, our alpha machines were
all at RedHat 5.2 (glibc 2.0.7, ypbind version 3.3-glibc3).  Since
posting my first query in this newsgroup, I then went back to the 
NIS HOWTO, re-read section 6.8.3 on PAM, and re-implemented all 
the changes for exchanging pam_pwdb with the corresponding pam_unix_* 
module throughout all the PAM files. NIS worked this time!  Perhaps 
in my earlier testing I only changed the rlogin PAM file, thinking
to just make minimal changes enough to let the NIS password be
accepted  -- changing *all* the PAM files wherever pam_pwdb appeared
let NIS ids & shadow passwords to be accepted.  So, the solution
was already outlined in the NIS HOWTO, I just didn't follow it
correctly.

To further test the needed PAM changes & RedHat 5.2, we ended up
upgrading one machine to RedHat 6.0, and now NIS & shadow passwords
work without the pam_pwdb/pam_unix_* substitution (PAM changes are not
needed under RedHat 6.0).

Thanks everyone for their time,

Fran Lawas-Grodek

