On Tue, 2 Nov 1999 19:28:31 -0600, LordCompaq <kimntodd@dont-spam-me.execpc.com>
wrote:
>So far, it seems that there are two little trays in the front. What are
>these for? Micro CD's? 2.5" harddrives (like a laptop)?

These trays can be used to hold a 2.5" (laptop) IDE hard drive and a floppy
drive simultaneously.

>
>Mine has a SCSI controller (weak little card, actually) with a 50 pin
>connector and a drive tray that takes up the expansion slot. 

It is my undrestanding that the Multia models with the SCSI controller can't
take regular PCI cards for space constraint issues. I could be wrong. In any
case, the idea is that you can put a 3.5" SCSI-2 drive back there.

>What else can
>be used here? Video....NIC...? 

Since there is on-board video and NIC, there isn't too much of a necessity to
use 3rd-party products.

>
>There is also the issue of the connectors behind the "cage" in the front of
>the board. It seems that there is an IDE-like connector, and an orifice for
>a ribbon.  What are these for?

The mini-IDE connector is for the laptop-sized hard drive (I hear the little
IDE cables can be hard to find), and the ribbon orifice is for the little
floppy drive (also laptop-like, I think).

As far as I know, all of these things work ok with linux.

Hope this helps,

John Burg
