Dear All,

The laboratory where I work purchased new computer
with Alpha 21164A, 600 MHz and preinstalled LINUX
RedHat. Surprisingly we found that the real
velocity for floating point operation is twice
slower than we expected from SPECfp (the value
27.0 was advertised, but really it is near the
13..15, almost the same as PII-450 MHz) - it was
found running Fortran program, compiled with DEC
Fortran on the same Alpha 21164 (DEC UNIX) and
Linux Fortran.

Sail-manager from company where we bought it said
(after purchasing :-) that twice slower floating
point performance (against DEC UNIX and DEC
Fortran) is a natural thing of LINUX for Alpha
processor.

Is it really so and if there is way to accelerate
our computer with LINUX (free of charge preferable
:))?

Thank you for any commence,

Dmitriy


